<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Malay Regiment</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1933–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Malay Regiment</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal Malay Regiment is the main infantry regiment of the Malaysian Army, founded by the British in 1933 as the Malay Regiment. It fought against the Japanese invasion of 1941–1942, notably at Pasir Panjang in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, and against communist insurgents in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malayan-emergency">Malayan Emergency</a>, and was granted the title 'Royal' in 1960.</p></div>
